@startuml configuration-publication
title Configuration publication - CIP-0002 Draft v4; CIP-0006 narrow acceptance / v4 pending; CIP-0004 accepted no-source-v1 target
actor "Operator / granted agent\napproval within ceiling" as O
participant "Curator manager\noperator UID; protected authority" as M
database "Manager-owned records/store\nregistration, approval, composition, lease\nprofile_settings, prior-key values, journal, marker" as S
participant "Shared launch construction\ncaller-side curator-run + agents-management; caller UID" as L
participant "Destination executor\nexecution UID bound by launch; agent-account curator-run for broker\nSH2 swarma-session-runner later; native child launched from plan" as H
participant "Generated interactive hook\nuser shell process" as SH
database "Hook cache\nmanager-owned generation bytes/options\nloaded snapshot belongs to shell" as C

== CIP-0002 project-context proposal; no adopted home/transform grammar ==
O -> M: register / inspect / preview / approve selected snapshot digest
M -> M: bounded untrusted inventory; canonical registered CWD; no execution/imported authority
break unreadable/malformed input, self-minted approval, ceiling violation or unsupported required semantics
  M --> O: refuse; no fragment or child
end
M -> S: protected snapshot + approval; compose project over selected profile lock
M -> M: identical pins dedupe; whole-skill replacement; unique command/MCP owners
break incompatible requirements, ambiguous owner, revoked approval or unproved native discovery exclusion
  M --> O: refuse composition / strict capability
end
M -> S: preparation: inspect composition and existing session leases before publication
alt changed composition with live lease
  S --> M: project_view_busy: wait or refuse; never switch files beneath session
else live or indeterminate session after crash/detach
  S --> M: retain lease/home/artifacts; recover process/session identity before collection
else idle admitted view
  M -> S: acquire lease before collection; revalidate; publish generated surfaces under transaction
  M -> L: metadata-only context/lease + typed command transform (v4 proposal)
  L -> H: immutable composed plan; destination admits child environment
  H -> H: D-PATH: protected tool prefix; admitted base order; one protected dispatcher
  note right of H
    Deduplicate by identity; preserve existing dispatcher position in base,
    otherwise append. No repository .agents/bin; no recreation of excluded PATH.
    Bind context/transform/resolved PATH into effective plan digest.
  end note
  break unsupported consumer, absent/excluded PATH, changed destination context or unreadable state
    H --> L: refuse before child; resume must reproduce pinned effective plan
  end
end
note over M,S
  Stable checkout x profile x environment home is recommended, still open.
  Pure preview starts no child and acquires no durable launch lease.
  Lease transfers to actual tracked session/runner before caller exit; descendants/detach retain it.
end note

== CIP-0006 machine declaration and per-home application are separate ==
O -> M: full closed profile_settings record/map; explicit global/project scope and false/empty values
M -> M: strict decode and adapter/scope checks before atomic config write
break malformed/unsupported input or wrong project binding
  M --> O: refuse; no declaration/home mutation
end
M -> S: atomically publish declaration; home may intentionally remain stale
O -> M: env resolve --repair; takeover consent when acquiring a conflicting key
M -> S: read managed base + owned-key projection + prior values under lock/journal
break failed parse/read, owned drift without repair, no takeover or concurrent file change
  M --> O: refuse; never use an empty base or replace unrelated keys
end
M -> M: plan complete candidate; keep unrelated keys, presence and source scope
M -> M: MCP absent inherits; denied wins; disabled remains explicit even with no positives
alt pinned adapter proves negative suppression
  M -> S: publish exact managed keys + marker/effective digest; journal recovery on failed mutation
  M -> L: v4 metadata + explicit MCP policy/channel
  L -> H: Claude canonical empty set + strict flag; Codex qualified per-name suppression
else source class / Codex encoding unsupported
  M --> O: mcp_policy_unenforceable; no permissive fragment/launch
end
O -> M: unset/release owned keys
alt current key equals last managed value
  M -> S: restore saved prior value/absence; preserve unrelated provider edits
else key changed
  M --> O: provider_settings_release_conflict; preserve current data
end
note over M,S
  Per-home journal recovery; outer importer compensates failed multi-profile rollout.
  No all-homes atomicity. Exact new schema bounds and rollback record encoding
  unspecified in spec CIP-0006 Specification changes; v1-v3 remain frozen.
end note

== CIP-0004 interactive activation; independent from project admission ==
O -> M: refresh/install existing managed hook cache; retain include_global option
M -> C: canonical no-source-v1 bytes + proposed generation metadata
alt unknown/custom/unreadable or partial cache
  M --> O: legacy/unknown/non-current; explicit regeneration; no inferred live-shell update
else user reloads or starts fresh shell
  C -> SH: load trusted generated hook
  SH -> SH: enter/switch/leave: restore owned prior PATH snapshot; clear old root/state
  SH -> SH: metadata-only nearest .agents discovery; no env/Skillfile/approval reads
  alt invalid/inaccessible/indeterminate discovery or unrepresentable path
    SH -> SH: disable affected activation scope; no fallback to another project
  else valid discovered scope
    SH -> SH: literal assignments: inherited PATH -> optional global -> optional project
  end
  SH -> SH: CURATOR_AUTO_ENV=0: clear project; retain only enabled global; never source files
end
note over SH,C
  Shell snapshot is transient. Cached bytes/options persist; legacy approvals give no authority.
  Loaded old functions require reload/restart; live state unknown unless observed.
